  "question": {
    "text": "A black body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>34</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>38</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and surface area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is at an initial temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. It is allowed to cool inside an evacuated enclosure kept at constant temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The rate of cooling is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The specific heat of the body in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is<br />\r(Stefan's constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.73</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
